      "writtenOn": "2024-09-23T17:58:08Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It depends on the setup. This `#else` block is in fact the only block that is currently built on our builders, as `__ANDROID_API__` is the targeted minimum API level and our builders are setting this to 16, 19, or 26 (Skia claims to support back to 4.3, API 19). This `#else` block kicks in when the minimum target is before R. If the minimum target is R or later then we use the first block and just use the NDK directly instead of looking for the symbols at runtime. Note that Chrome still supports back to Oreo (Android 8 / API 26) so will also get this `#else` block for now (if they use it).",
      "parentUuid": "203f5a25_47282a67",
      "revId": "9baab71b4862cd3be1192632dd475a6c50171af4",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
